{:mulog/duration 156500, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.event-store-v3.core.in-memory", :grain/event-ids (#uuid "019e4323-91db-7012-9f2a-978ea8e42b7f" #uuid "019e4323-91da-70f5-906c-5265114d26dd"), :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YxN-v-I7Or7Uk9TG5rUkFQoUwGets", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YxN-v-I7Or7Uk9TG5rUkFQoUwGets", :mulog/timestamp 1779242865116, :metric/name "GrainAppendEvents", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YxN0MazDUadcKr6J3SfDipA7ErhjW", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.event-store-v3.core.in-memory/append}
{:mulog/duration 2084291, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/command {:tick-id #uuid "c6e5142c-e2ec-4320-bcfa-db1bacb5f74e", :writes {:document-survey "### Side-by-Side Structure Overview\n\n| Section / Appendix | Contract v2.0 | Contract v3.1.1 | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Part 1 – Contract Details** | Included | Included | Layout and core fields remain consistent. |\n| Section A: Contract/Supplier Info | Included | Included | Item A(11) in v3 adds \"Prescribed Form\" requirement. |\n| Section B: Facility Characteristics | Included | Included | Item B(5)(iv) [Domestic Content] **Removed** in v3. |\n| Section C: Documents Included | Included | Included | Content remains the same. |\n| **Part 2 – General Terms** | Included | Included | Major sections (1-14) are identical in title. |\n| Section 4: Representations | Included | Included | 4.4.4 [Domestic Content] **Removed** in v3. |\n| Section 6.5: Info Collection | Included | Included | v3 adds disclosure for public health/safety/emergency. |\n| **Appendix A: Definitions** | Included | Included | v3 adds \"Prescribed Form\" and \"Website\" definitions. |\n| **Appendix B: Indexed Price** | Included | Included | Formula and calculation logic are identical. |\n| **Appendix C: Solar PV** | Included | Included | **Significant Content Removal** in v3 (see below). |\n| **Appendix D-1: Directly Conn.** | Included | Included | Content is identical. |\n| **Appendix D-2: Indirectly Conn.**| Included | Included | Content is identical. |\n| **Appendix E: LDC Supplier** | Included | Included | Content is identical. |\n\n---\n\n### Analysis of Changes\n\n#### 1. New Sections / Definitions (v3.1.1)\n*   **Prescribed Form:** A new definition in Appendix A of v3.1.1 requires that notices (Section 7.2), terminations (Section 8.1), and amendments (Section 9) use the latest version of forms found on the OPA Website.\n*   **Website:** Formally defined in Appendix A of v3.1.1 to provide a specific URL for program resources.\n*   **Emergency Disclosure:** Section 6.5 in v3.1.1 includes a new provision allowing the OPA to disclose facility details to government ministries/agencies for the purposes of public health, safety, and emergency response planning.\n\n#### 2. Missing / Removed Sections (v3.1.1)\n*   **Domestic Content Requirements:** \n    *   **Part 1, B(5)(iv):** The field for \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" is removed in v3.1.1.\n    *   **Part 2, 4.4.4:** The representation that the facility meets a specific Domestic Content Level is removed.\n    *   **Appendix C (Solar PV Schedule):** In v2.0, Appendix C contains extensive sections (1.1 through 1.7) and three detailed tables (Crystalline Silicon, Thin-Film, and Concentrated PV) regarding domestic content qualifying percentages. **All these tables and the associated calculation rules are removed in v3.1.1.**\n*   **Rooftop Definition:** In Appendix C, the definition of \"Existing Building\" was expanded in v3.1.1 to allow OPA discretion to \"deem\" a building as an Existing Building.\n\n#### 3. Structural Consistency\nDespite the significant removal of the Renewable Energy Domestic Content rules, the alphanumeric numbering of the main Contract Parts (1 and 2) and the Appendices (A through E) remains synchronized between both versions."}, :command/name :sheet/complete-node-execution, :command/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:07:45.114138-05:00", :command/id #uuid "0e852bf9-c088-4a26-9600-28081c49e6d5", :duration-ms 6012, :usage {:prompt-tokens 25430, :completion-tokens 815, :total-tokens 26245}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "f9396da3-d598-41bd-82d0-630f7d06eac9", :sheet-id #uuid "345df149-dae9-48af-91ae-493c5ee1486e"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YxN-v-I7Or7Uk9TG5rUkFQoUwGets", :mulog/timestamp 1779242865114, :metric/name "CommandProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YxN-v-I7Or7Uk9TG5rUkFQoUwGets", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.command-processor-v2.core/process-command, :metric/resolution :high}
{:mulog/parent-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YxN0TsBc_FJ0DiG8Azq6fU4YN9tdr", :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YxN0TsBc_FJ0DiG8Azq6fU4YN9tdr", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3YxN0UtXsLFMRXS6hIsvKHpzniFUix", :mulog/timestamp 1779242865116, :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/anomaly-in-todo-processor, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :anomaly {:cognitect.anomalies/category :cognitect.anomalies/fault, :cognitect.anomalies/message "Todo Processor returned nil: %s"}}
{:mulog/duration 70792, :mulog/namespace "ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core", :mulog/outcome :ok, :mulog/parent-trace nil, :event {:tick-id #uuid "c6e5142c-e2ec-4320-bcfa-db1bacb5f74e", :writes {:document-survey "### Side-by-Side Structure Overview\n\n| Section / Appendix | Contract v2.0 | Contract v3.1.1 | Notes |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Part 1 – Contract Details** | Included | Included | Layout and core fields remain consistent. |\n| Section A: Contract/Supplier Info | Included | Included | Item A(11) in v3 adds \"Prescribed Form\" requirement. |\n| Section B: Facility Characteristics | Included | Included | Item B(5)(iv) [Domestic Content] **Removed** in v3. |\n| Section C: Documents Included | Included | Included | Content remains the same. |\n| **Part 2 – General Terms** | Included | Included | Major sections (1-14) are identical in title. |\n| Section 4: Representations | Included | Included | 4.4.4 [Domestic Content] **Removed** in v3. |\n| Section 6.5: Info Collection | Included | Included | v3 adds disclosure for public health/safety/emergency. |\n| **Appendix A: Definitions** | Included | Included | v3 adds \"Prescribed Form\" and \"Website\" definitions. |\n| **Appendix B: Indexed Price** | Included | Included | Formula and calculation logic are identical. |\n| **Appendix C: Solar PV** | Included | Included | **Significant Content Removal** in v3 (see below). |\n| **Appendix D-1: Directly Conn.** | Included | Included | Content is identical. |\n| **Appendix D-2: Indirectly Conn.**| Included | Included | Content is identical. |\n| **Appendix E: LDC Supplier** | Included | Included | Content is identical. |\n\n---\n\n### Analysis of Changes\n\n#### 1. New Sections / Definitions (v3.1.1)\n*   **Prescribed Form:** A new definition in Appendix A of v3.1.1 requires that notices (Section 7.2), terminations (Section 8.1), and amendments (Section 9) use the latest version of forms found on the OPA Website.\n*   **Website:** Formally defined in Appendix A of v3.1.1 to provide a specific URL for program resources.\n*   **Emergency Disclosure:** Section 6.5 in v3.1.1 includes a new provision allowing the OPA to disclose facility details to government ministries/agencies for the purposes of public health, safety, and emergency response planning.\n\n#### 2. Missing / Removed Sections (v3.1.1)\n*   **Domestic Content Requirements:** \n    *   **Part 1, B(5)(iv):** The field for \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" is removed in v3.1.1.\n    *   **Part 2, 4.4.4:** The representation that the facility meets a specific Domestic Content Level is removed.\n    *   **Appendix C (Solar PV Schedule):** In v2.0, Appendix C contains extensive sections (1.1 through 1.7) and three detailed tables (Crystalline Silicon, Thin-Film, and Concentrated PV) regarding domestic content qualifying percentages. **All these tables and the associated calculation rules are removed in v3.1.1.**\n*   **Rooftop Definition:** In Appendix C, the definition of \"Existing Building\" was expanded in v3.1.1 to allow OPA discretion to \"deem\" a building as an Existing Building.\n\n#### 3. Structural Consistency\nDespite the significant removal of the Renewable Energy Domestic Content rules, the alphanumeric numbering of the main Contract Parts (1 and 2) and the Appendices (A through E) remains synchronized between both versions."}, :duration-ms 6012, :event/tags #{[:tick #uuid "c6e5142c-e2ec-4320-bcfa-db1bacb5f74e"] [:node #uuid "f9396da3-d598-41bd-82d0-630f7d06eac9"] [:sheet #uuid "345df149-dae9-48af-91ae-493c5ee1486e"]}, :event/timestamp #time/offset-date-time "2026-05-19T21:07:45.114771-05:00", :usage {:prompt-tokens 25430, :completion-tokens 815, :total-tokens 26245}, :status :success, :node-id #uuid "f9396da3-d598-41bd-82d0-630f7d06eac9", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-completed, :sheet-id #uuid "345df149-dae9-48af-91ae-493c5ee1486e", :event/id #uuid "019e4323-91da-70f5-906c-5265114d26dd"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3YxN0TsBc_F