tative information. (Citation: Section 5.1.2)\n*   **Section 6.5 - Collection/Disclosure of Information:**\n    *   **Modified:** Reference to \"information to establish compliance with Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" has been **removed**. (Citation: Section 6.5, first paragraph)\n    *   **Addition:** Added a new purpose for disclosure: \"promoting public health and safety and allowing emergency services personnel, as well as other public officials to plan and respond properly in the event of an emergency.\" (Citation: Section 6.5, Disclosure of Information paragraph)\n*   **Section 7.2 - Change of Contact Info:** Modified to require notice \"in the **Prescribed Form**.\" (Citation: Section 7.2)\n*   **Section 8.1 - Termination:** Modified to require notice \"in the **Prescribed Form**.\" (Citation: Section 8.1)\n*   **Section 9 - Amendment:** Modified to require amendments be \"reduced to writing in the **Prescribed Form**.\" (Citation: Section 9)\n\n### 4. Appendix A: Definitions\n*   **Removed Definitions:**\n    *   \"Abut\" (Note: Though \"Abut\" appears in the text of Appendix A in both, the specific Domestic Content related definitions are impacted).\n    *   \"Domestic Content Level\" (Removed)\n    *   \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" (Removed)\n*   **Added Definitions:**\n    *   \"Prescribed Form\" (Added): Refers to the latest version of forms on the Website.\n    *   \"Website\" (Added): Defines the microFIT URL.\n*   **Modified Definitions:**\n    *   \"Project Eligibility Requirements\": Requirement (c) now includes a qualifier: \"**unless otherwise consented to by the OPA in writing in its sole and absolute discretion**.\" (Citation: Appendix A, Project Eligibility Requirements)\n\n### 5. Appendix C: Solar Photovoltaic Schedule\n*   **Definition - Existing Building:** Expanded to include a new clause (b) allowing OPA \"in its sole and absolute discretion\" to issue written confirmation deeming a building an Existing Building. (Citation: Appendix C, Section 1)\n*   **Domestic Content Requirements:** Sections 1.1 through 1.7 and the associated Tables (Table 1: Crystalline Silicon; Table 2: Thin-Film; Table 3: Concentrated PV) have been **completely removed**. Version 3.1.1 contains no domestic content grids or qualifying percentage rules.\n\n### 6. Appendices B, D-1, D-2, and E\n*   **Unchanged:** These sections remain substantively identical, with minor formatting adjustments.", :major-changes "### MAJOR (Legal/Financial Impact)\n*   **Removal of Domestic Content Requirements:** Significant change across multiple sections (Part 1 Section B(5)(iv), Part 2 Section 4.4.4, Section 6.5, and Appendix C). The removal of the \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" and the associated warranty and data tables is a substantial shift in project eligibility and compliance risk for the Supplier.\n*   **Definition Removal:** Deletion of \"Domestic Content Level\" and \"Minimum Required Domestic Content Level\" from Appendix A, stripping the contract of previous regulatory thresholds.\n*   **Project Eligibility Modification:** The definition of \"Project Eligibility Requirements\" in Appendix A now includes a discretionary qualifier allowing the OPA to grant consent in its \"sole and absolute discretion,\" potentially impacting the enforcement of eligibility.\n*   **Building Criteria Modification:** Appendix C Section 1 now grants the OPA \"sole and absolute discretion\" to deem a structure an \"Existing Building,\" providing more flexibility in project classification.\n*   **Information Disclosure Expansion:** Section 6.5 now includes an additional legal basis for information disclosure related to public health, safety, and emergency planning.\n\n### MINOR (Clarification)\n*   **Notification Protocol:** Sections 5.1.2, 7.2, 8.1, and 9 now mandate the use of the \"Prescribed Form\" for notifications, terminations, and amendments.\n*   **New Definitions:** Addition of \"Prescribed Form\" and \"Website\" in Appendix A to clarify administrative processes and form locations.\n*   **Section Renumbering:** Sections 4.4.5 and 4.4.6 were renumbered to 4.4.4 and 4.4.5 respectively following the deletion of the Domestic Content Warranty.\n\n### COSMETIC (Formatting)\n*   **Version Update:** Contract version updated from 2.0 to 3.1.1 on Pages 1 and 5.\n*   **General Typography:** Minor corrections to punctuation, spacing, and standardized indentation throughout the document.\n*   **Pagination:** Re-pagination of Part 1 Section B following the removal of subsection 5."}, :node-id #uuid "7b6af257-3aea-4706-ab42-96fb62cf11c3", :event/type :sheet/node-execution-started, :sheet-id #uuid "345df149-dae9-48af-91ae-493c5ee1486e", :event/id #uuid "019e4323-bdef-70e8-b275-27a1476d2fd7"}, :mulog/root-trace #mulog/flake "5A3Yy12fKpRZKGrGExy1E-WWbfO8sv7P", :mulog/timestamp 1779242876400, :metric/name "TodoProcessed", :mulog/trace-id #mulog/flake "5A3Yy12fKpRZKGrGExy1E-WWbfO8sv7P", :mulog/event-name :ai.obney.grain.todo-processor-v2.core/processing-event, :metric/resolution :high}
